1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,834
A Jira issue can be done while the promise behind it is still

2
00:00:03,834 --> 00:00:08,289
at risk. Promisory connects work to an accepted owner, an agreed deadline,
and

3
00:00:08,289 --> 00:00:09,660
evidence of the outcome.

4
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:13,591
This is the installed Forge app on our test site.

5
00:00:13,591 --> 00:00:17,843
A reopened blocking bug appears in the owner's inbox, linked to the affected

6
00:00:17,843 --> 00:00:18,458
commitment.

7
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:24,464
Jira's hierarchy stays intact. Stories, tasks, and bugs remain peers;

8
00:00:24,464 --> 00:00:26,391
blockers are dependencies.

9
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:32,134
The lifecycle view connects goals, initiatives, and Confluence requirements.

10
00:00:32,134 --> 00:00:37,736
The PRD revision, requirement mapping, and release readiness gate have
separate versions.

11
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:45,174
Rovo reads the same permitted evidence and identifies the current blocker.

12
00:00:45,174 --> 00:00:49,615
It can explain or draft, while review and execution remain explicit steps in

13
00:00:49,615 --> 00:00:50,083
the app.

14
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:57,626
A separate reviewer account approves this exact proposal: move test issue
KAN seven

15
00:00:57,626 --> 00:01:00,388
from November twenty fourth to the twenty fifth.

16
00:01:00,388 --> 00:01:02,690
The commitment deadline stays unchanged.

17
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:11,387
When we apply, the executor checks current evidence and Decionis authority
before Jira

18
00:01:11,387 --> 00:01:15,077
receives the write. Watch the result change to Change verified.

19
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:30,323
Jira is read again, and the authority record is saved.

20
00:01:30,323 --> 00:01:34,616
The evidence binds the action to its intent hash and reviewed source
revision.

21
00:01:36,350 --> 00:01:38,793
This separate, existing request is blocked.

22
00:01:38,793 --> 00:01:43,054
An unresolved claim cannot be treated as permission to try the write again.

23
00:01:43,850 --> 00:01:47,543
Finally, the designated verifier accepts the agreed evidence.

24
00:01:47,543 --> 00:01:50,146
Only then does the outcome become verified.

25
00:01:50,146 --> 00:01:54,565
The original promise date remains visible when the Jira due date changes.

26
00:02:00,850 --> 00:02:06,240
The ledger shows three verified outcomes, including one delivered after its
original date.

27
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,857
History survives revisions.

28
00:02:08,850 --> 00:02:11,480
Judges can install the separate judge app.

29
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:14,862
Successful governed writes run on the bound test site.

30
00:02:14,862 --> 00:02:18,558
Promisory: see risk, act within limits, and prove delivery.
